  "preamble": "Stressed open-mid [ɔ] breaks into a rising diphthong [wɔ] with a labial-velar onglide. In Tuscan and Standard Italian, Latin short ŏ, pronounced [ɔ] already in Classical Latin, became uo in stressed open syllables (bonus > buono, focus > fuoco), while it stayed [ɔ] in closed syllables (porta > porta).",
